+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The repo is a blank Godot project — the first playable vertical slice (E1: tiny planet + orbit camera + connect verb, NO sim, NO character) does not exist yet.
+
+**Approach:** Bootstrap the Godot 4.7.1 project and build the slice from the epic's five stories: seeded wedge planet with geodesic surface math, view-layer orbit camera with zoom ladder, positional draw/orbit disambiguation with the connect verb, geodesic pipe arcs with strand bundles + parallel merge, and chunky primitive node buildings — look-parity with the little-planet reference (palette tokens + flat shading only, IP guardrail).
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Test contracts from the epic hold: snap honors intent not path; arcs are valid geodesics (no tunneling); draw-vs-orbit never misfires; camera never rolls; NO sim state exists (presentation + input only).
+- All wedge layout, node placement, and decor derive from a single seed (deterministic; owned RNG — no wall-clock).
+- Look-parity tokens only: flat-shaded low-poly primitives, GDD palette range (space `#16243a`, grass `#5fae5f`, sand `#d9c07a`, water `#3fb8af`, arctic `#dfe8ee`); saturated accents reserved for network elements.
+- Scenes stay text `.tscn`/`.tres`; world-gen lives in seeded GDScript (planet mesh built at runtime from seed — the seed, not baked mesh data, is the source of truth).
+- Snap radius measured in surface arc (zoom-independent feel).
+
+**Ask First:**
+- Any deviation from the epic's story/contract list, or any need for third-party assets/addons.
+
+**Never:**
+- No flow simulation, packets, tick engine, demand, health, or any sim state (E2+).
+- No copying of the reference video's assets/layout/identity (look only).
+- No purchased/licensed assets; no non-primitive custom meshes; no textures.
+- No character controller, no minimap, no limb markers, no QoS lanes semantics (strand rendering is presentation-only in E1).
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Draw happy path | Press on node A, drag across surface, release within snap radius of node B | Preview arc follows pointer surface-projection; on release, pipe commits between A and B | N/A |
+| Cancel | Press on node A, drag, release on empty surface (outside every snap radius) | No pipe created; preview disappears | N/A |
+| Snap honors intent | Release far from the drag's geometric endpoint but within snap arc of node B | Connects to B (min surface-arc distance within radius), not to the raw release point | No node in radius → cancel |
+| Orbit vs draw | Press on empty surface/sky vs press on a node | Empty = orbit drag; node = draw drag; one positional rule, no modes | N/A |
+| Latitude clamp | Drag orbit past the pole | Pitch clamps at ±85°; up-vector stable; zero roll at every azimuth | N/A |
+| Zoom ladder | Scroll/pinch | Altitude eases between globe/district/street stops (damped), never continuous drift | N/A |
+| Antipodal-ish arc | Connect two nodes ~180° apart | Path still a valid great-circle geodesic (deterministic axis choice); elevated, never below surface | Deterministic perpendicular axis |
+| Parallel pipes | Draw a second pipe between an already-connected pair | Both render as one fatter merged bundle at the same geodesic path | N/A |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
+
