+- [x] `scripts/node_site.gd` -- primitive buildings oriented to surface normal, seeded placement with min angular separation on wedges -- E1.5
+- [x] `scripts/orbit_camera.gd` -- drag-orbit + clamp + damping + zoom ladder -- E1.2
+- [x] `scripts/input_router.gd` + `scripts/connect_controller.gd` -- positional disambiguation, preview arc, snap, commit/cancel -- E1.3
+- [x] `scripts/pipe_arc.gd` -- elevated geodesic cable, 3 strands, trestles, parallel-merge-fatter registry -- E1.4
+- [x] `scripts/hud.gd` + `README.md` -- hint chip + run command -- A2
+- [x] `tests/*` -- headless suite covering every epic test contract -- A1
+- [x] `scripts/capture_runner.gd` + `captures/` -- the four committed captures -- A4
+- [x] Godot MCP loop: `lsp-diagnostics` clean on all GDScript; `editor-run` + `debug-output` boot check, iterate on errors -- A3
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given the project is run (`godot --path <root>`), when the main scene loads, then the planet renders with 3 distinct biome wedges + turquoise water ring in deep-navy space, at 60 fps on desktop.
+- Given the headless suite runs (`godot --headless -s res://tests/run_tests.gd`), when it completes, then every epic test contract passes: snap-intent, geodesic validity (no sample below surface, path on the great-circle plane), disambiguation classification, zero camera roll across full azimuth × clamped-pitch sweeps, and no sim state/group in the tree.
+- Given a drag starting on node A, when released within snap arc of node B, then pipe A–B commits; when released elsewhere, then nothing commits.
+- Given two pipes drawn between the same node pair, when the second commits, then the bundle renders as one fatter cable on the same geodesic path.
+- Given `captures/` at PR time, when inspected, then it contains the four required captures matching the in-game look (chunky flat-shaded, little-planet palette).
+- Given `lsp-diagnostics` over all scripts, when run, then zero errors/warnings.
